  '{1}',
  'Option B (To group similar data points together without prior labels) is the correct answer. Clustering is an unsupervised learning technique used to partition data into groups (clusters) where data points within a cluster are more similar to each other than to those in other clusters. Option A describes classification. Option C describes regression or forecasting. Option D is anomaly detection, which can sometimes use clustering but is a distinct goal.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  8,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_1',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

