VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_1_39',
  'Which of the following best describes a ''Foundation Model''?',
  'mcq',
  '["A machine learning model specifically trained for image classification tasks.","A model that is trained from scratch for every new task.","A large ML model trained on a vast quantity of data at scale, designed to be adaptable to a wide range of downstream tasks.","A small, specialized model used for edge device inference."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) accurately describes a Foundation Model. These are large-scale machine learning models, often deep learning models, trained on broad data (unlabeled and/or labeled) that can be adapted (fine-tuned) to a wide range of downstream tasks, rather than being trained for a single specific task. Option A is too specific. Option B is incorrect as foundation models are designed for adaptability, not retraining from scratch. Option D describes a lightweight model, often the opposite of a foundation model.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  15,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

