  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) accurately defines the relationship: AI is the broad concept of machines simulating human intelligence, encompassing various techniques. Machine Learning is a specific subset of AI that focuses on enabling systems to learn from data through statistical methods, without being explicitly programmed for every task. Option A is incorrect as it reverses the hierarchy; ML is a subset of AI. Option C is incorrect; ML includes supervised, unsupervised, and reinforcement learning. Option D is incorrect; AI is a field, and ML is a paradigm within it, not a specific algorithm.',
