  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) indicates when AI/ML is appropriate: when patterns are too complex for explicit rules. Anomaly detection often involves subtle deviations that are difficult to hard-code. Option A describes a scenario where traditional rule-based logic is sufficient and more cost-effective. Option C suggests that AI/ML is appropriate even when costs outweigh benefits, which is incorrect. Option D also points to traditional programming being more suitable if it can solve the problem reliably with less complexity.',
