  'Option C (correct) defines the context window, which is the limit on how much text (input prompt, conversation history, and generated response) a foundation model can consider at one time. Exceeding this limit can lead to truncation or errors. Option A refers to scalability. Option B refers to model size. Option D refers to deployment region.',
