  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) highlights the key advantages of smaller models: they typically have lower inference latency and are more cost-effective to run, especially for tasks where their performance is sufficient (anti-pattern ap-3.1-001). Option A is not necessarily true; creativity is controlled by parameters like temperature. Option B is incorrect; smaller models often require less data for fine-tuning. Option D is generally false; larger models often have larger context windows.',
