VALUES (
  'q_7_m_7_1_37',
  'A company needs to build a chatbot that answers questions based on its internal, proprietary documentation, ensuring responses are always factual and current. Which approach is MOST suitable for this requirement with Amazon Bedrock?',
  'mcq',
  '["Fine-tuning a general-purpose foundation model on the internal documentation.","Using Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) with Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases linked to the documentation.","Prompting a large, general-purpose model with zero-shot instructions.","Continuously pre-training a foundation model from scratch with the internal documentation."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) is the most suitable approach. RAG with Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases allows the model to retrieve and incorporate up-to-date information from proprietary sources, ensuring grounded and factual responses without altering the model''s weights. Option A (fine-tuning) is less ideal for frequently updated information and can be costly for large datasets. Option C (zero-shot prompting) would not provide access to proprietary knowledge. Option D (continued pre-training) is overly complex and expensive for this use case.',
