  'Option A (correct) is the most cost-effective choice. For simple tasks, smaller models often achieve comparable accuracy at significantly lower cost and latency. Option B is an anti-pattern (ap-3.1-001) as larger models cost more per token and have higher latency. Options C and D introduce unnecessary complexity and cost for a simple text classification task.',
