  '["The dataset must be extremely small to prevent overfitting.","The data must be low-quality and uncurated to challenge the model.","The data must be high-quality, diverse, and representative of the target task.","The dataset should only contain examples that the base model already handles well."]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) emphasizes the importance of high-quality, diverse, and representative data for effective fine-tuning. The quality of fine-tuning is proportional to the training data quality (anti-pattern ap-3.3-001). Option A is incorrect; very small datasets can lead to overfitting. Option B is an anti-pattern (ap-3.3-001) and would lead to poor performance. Option D would not help the model learn new capabilities or address its weaknesses.',
