VALUES (
  'q_7_m_7_3_31',
  'What is the primary benefit of Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning (PEFT) techniques like LoRA?',
  'mcq',
  '["They enable models to generate multi-modal outputs.","They allow fine-tuning of large models with significantly fewer trainable parameters and computational resources.","They completely eliminate the need for any pre-training data.","They ensure the model always produces deterministic outputs."]'::json,
  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) describes the core benefit of PEFT techniques like LoRA: they make fine-tuning large foundation models much more efficient by only updating a small subset of parameters, reducing memory, compute, and storage requirements. Option A is about model modality. Option C is incorrect; PEFT builds upon pre-trained models. Option D is incorrect; output determinism is controlled by inference parameters like temperature.',
