  'Option B (Its internal workings are difficult to interpret) is the defining characteristic of a ''black-box'' AI model. Deep neural networks, for example, often have complex, non-linear structures that make it challenging to understand how they arrive at a particular decision. Options A and C describe transparent models, and Option D is not universally true.',
