  '{0}'::int[],
  'Option A (SHAP values) is a widely used post-hoc explainability technique that helps to explain the output of any machine learning model by computing the contribution of each feature to an individual prediction. Options B (Decision trees) and C (Linear regression) are types of transparent models themselves, not post-hoc techniques for complex models. Option D (K-means clustering) is an unsupervised learning algorithm.',
