  'Option D (Implementing post-hoc explainability techniques) is essential when using complex ''black-box'' models like deep learning for regulated tasks. These techniques, such as SHAP values or feature importance, allow for justification of individual predictions without sacrificing model performance, which is often superior in complex models. Options A, B, and C would likely fail to meet the audit requirements for justification.',
