  '{2}',
  'Option C (Creating and maintaining Model Cards and Datasheets for the model and its data) is essential for comprehensive documentation. Model Cards detail the model''s purpose, development, and performance, while Datasheets document the characteristics of the training data. This practice is crucial for auditability and transparency. Option A (Implementing strong IAM policies for data access) and Option B (Encrypting all model artifacts with AWS KMS) are security measures, not documentation practices. Option D (Deploying the model endpoint within a private Amazon VPC) is a network security measure.',
