  '{1}',
  'Option B (Identifying, assessing, and mitigating potential risks associated with AI model development and deployment) is the primary goal of model risk management. This includes risks like bias, fairness, explainability, security vulnerabilities, and compliance failures. Option A (Accelerating training times) and Option C (Reducing inference latency) are performance optimization goals. Option D (Maximizing model accuracy at all costs) can lead to overlooking critical ethical and fairness concerns, which are central to model risk management.',
