VALUES (
  'q_9_m_9_2_63',
  'A global company trains AI models using customer data, which must adhere to strict data residency requirements in different regions and have defined retention periods. Which AWS service feature helps manage the lifecycle and regional placement of data stored for AI workloads?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS IAM policies to restrict data access","Amazon S3 lifecycle policies and bucket configurations for regional storage","AWS KMS for data encryption","AWS CloudTrail for data access logging"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Amazon S3 lifecycle policies and bucket configurations for regional storage) is the correct choice. Amazon S3 allows you to choose the AWS Region where your data is stored, directly addressing data residency requirements. S3 lifecycle policies enable automated management of data retention, transitioning data to different storage classes or deleting it after a defined period, fulfilling retention requirements. Option A (AWS IAM policies) manage access, not residency or lifecycle. Option C (AWS KMS) handles encryption. Option D (AWS CloudTrail) logs access events.',
