  'Option A (Classification) is a common ML use case where a model predicts a categorical label (e.g., spam or not spam). Option B (Regression) is another common ML use case for predicting a continuous numerical value (e.g., house prices). Option C (Clustering) is an unsupervised ML technique used to group similar data points together. Option D (Database Administration) and Option E (Operating System Management) are IT operations tasks and not direct machine learning use cases, although ML could potentially be applied to optimize these processes.',
