  'Option B (Layers) and Option D (Neurons) are fundamental components of neural networks. Neural networks are structured into layers, with each layer containing multiple interconnected neurons (or nodes) that process and transform data. Option A (Deterministic Rule Sets) and Option C (Explicit Algorithms) describe traditional programming or rule-based systems, which are distinct from the learning paradigm of neural networks. Option E (Relational Database Tables) refers to a data storage structure, not a component of a neural network.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  12,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

