INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_63',
  'The machine learning development lifecycle involves several distinct stages. Which of the following are fundamental stages in a typical ML pipeline? (Select THREE.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Data collection","Model training","Deployment","Software compilation","Hardware assembly"]'::json,
  '{0,1,2}'::int[],
  'Option A (Data collection) is correct as it''s the initial step to gather relevant data for the model. Option B (Model training) is correct, involving feeding data to an algorithm to learn patterns. Option C (Deployment) is correct, making the trained model available for inference. Option D (Software compilation) is a general software development process, not specific to the ML pipeline. Option E (Hardware assembly) is a physical infrastructure task, unrelated to the ML pipeline stages.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  31,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_64',
  'Data preprocessing is a critical phase in the ML lifecycle that significantly impacts model performance. Which of the following are common activities performed during the data preprocessing stage? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Handling missing values","Feature scaling","Model deployment","Hyperparameter tuning","API gateway creation"]'::json,
  '{0,1}'::int[],
  'Option A (Handling missing values) is correct as it addresses incomplete data, which can degrade model performance, highlighting the importance of not skipping data preprocessing. Option B (Feature scaling) is correct as it normalizes the range of independent variables or features, which is crucial for many ML algorithms. Option C (Model deployment) occurs much later in the ML lifecycle. Option D (Hyperparameter tuning) is part of the model training and optimization phase. Option E (API gateway creation) is an infrastructure task for model deployment, not a data preprocessing activity.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  32,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_65',
  'Evaluating a machine learning model''s performance requires appropriate metrics, especially for classification tasks. Which of the following metrics are commonly used to assess classification models, particularly when dealing with imbalanced datasets? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Precision","Recall","Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)","Throughput","Latency"]'::json,
  '{0,1}'::int[],
  'Option A (Precision) is correct, measuring the proportion of true positive predictions among all positive predictions. Option B (Recall) is correct, measuring the proportion of true positive predictions among all actual positive instances. Both are crucial for classification, especially with imbalanced datasets where accuracy alone can be misleading, addressing the anti-pattern of optimizing for accuracy alone. Option C (Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)) is a common metric for regression models, not classification. Option D (Throughput) and Option E (Latency) are performance metrics related to the speed and capacity of a system, not model predictive quality.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  33,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_66',
  'The machine learning lifecycle does not end with model deployment. Continuous activities are necessary to maintain model effectiveness in production. Which of the following are essential post-deployment activities for an ML model? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Model monitoring","Retraining","Initial data collection","Feature engineering","Algorithm selection"]'::json,
  '{0,1}'::int[],
  'Option A (Model monitoring) is correct as it involves tracking model performance, data drift, and concept drift to detect degradation. Option B (Retraining) is correct, as models often need to be updated with new data to maintain accuracy over time due to changing patterns, addressing the anti-pattern of treating model deployment as the end of the lifecycle. Option C (Initial data collection) and Option D (Feature engineering) are early stages of the ML lifecycle. Option E (Algorithm selection) is part of the model training phase.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  34,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_67',
  'In the machine learning lifecycle, training and inference are distinct phases with different characteristics. Which of the following statements accurately describe the model training phase? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Uses historical data","Is typically resource-intensive","Applies the model to new, unseen data","Generates real-time predictions","Focuses on low-latency responses"]'::json,
  '{0,1}'::int[],
  'Option A (Uses historical data) is correct because models learn patterns and relationships from past data during training. Option B (Is typically resource-intensive) is correct, as training often requires significant computational power (e.g., GPUs) and time. Option C (Applies the model to new, unseen data), Option D (Generates real-time predictions), and Option E (Focuses on low-latency responses) describe the inference phase, where the trained model is used to make predictions on new data.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  35,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_68',
  'Model generalization is a key goal in machine learning, referring to a model''s ability to perform well on unseen data. Which of the following terms describe common issues related to a model''s generalization capability? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Overfitting","Underfitting","Data corruption","Network latency","Storage capacity"]'::json,
  '{0,1}'::int[],
  'Option A (Overfitting) is correct, occurring when a model learns the training data too well, including noise, and performs poorly on new data. Option B (Underfitting) is correct, occurring when a model is too simple to capture the underlying patterns in the training data and performs poorly on both training and new data. Option C (Data corruption) is a data quality issue, not directly a model generalization issue. Option D (Network latency) and Option E (Storage capacity) are infrastructure-related concerns, not issues with a model''s ability to generalize from data.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  36,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_69',
  'In the typical machine learning development lifecycle, which of the following are crucial stages that occur before model training? (Select THREE.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Data Collection","Model Deployment","Data Preprocessing","Feature Engineering","Model Monitoring"]'::json,
  '{0,2,3}'::int[],
  'Option A (Data Collection) is correct as it''s the initial step to gather relevant data for the ML project. Option C (Data Preprocessing) is correct, involving cleaning, transforming, and preparing the raw data. Option D (Feature Engineering) is also correct, as it involves creating new features or transforming existing ones to improve model performance. Option B (Model Deployment) and Option E (Model Monitoring) occur after the model has been trained and evaluated, making them post-training stages.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  37,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_70',
  'When evaluating a machine learning model, especially for classification tasks, which metrics are commonly used to assess its performance beyond simple accuracy, particularly in cases of class imbalance? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Precision","Recall","Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)","Mean Absolute Error (MAE)","Throughput"]'::json,
  '{0,1}'::int[],
  'Option A (Precision) is correct, measuring the proportion of true positive predictions among all positive predictions, which is crucial when false positives are costly. Option B (Recall) is also correct, measuring the proportion of true positive predictions among all actual positive instances, important when false negatives are costly. Option C (Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)) and Option D (Mean Absolute Error (MAE)) are common evaluation metrics for regression problems, not classification. Option E (Throughput) is a performance metric related to system capacity, not model prediction quality.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  38,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_71',
  'A machine learning specialist observes that their model performs exceptionally well on the training data but poorly on new, unseen data. Which of the following approaches can help address this issue? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Reduce the complexity of the model architecture.","Increase the amount of training data.","Increase the number of features significantly.","Train the model for more epochs without early stopping.","Use a more complex model architecture."]'::json,
  '{0,1}'::int[],
  'The scenario describes overfitting. Option A (Reduce the complexity of the model architecture) is correct because a simpler model is less likely to memorize the training data and generalize better to new data. Option B (Increase the amount of training data) is also correct, as providing more diverse examples helps the model learn more general patterns rather than specific noise in a smaller dataset. Option C (Increase the number of features significantly) could exacerbate overfitting by adding more noise or irrelevant information. Option D (Train the model for more epochs without early stopping) would likely worsen overfitting, as the model would continue to memorize the training data. Option E (Use a more complex model architecture) would also worsen overfitting, as complexity is a primary cause.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  39,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_72',
  'After deploying a machine learning model into production, a data science team must ensure its continued performance and relevance. Which of the following are essential post-deployment activities? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Continuous model monitoring for drift and performance degradation.","Regular retraining of the model with new data.","Skipping data preprocessing for new data streams.","Ceasing all model development once deployed.","Manually adjusting model predictions in real-time."]'::json,
  '{0,1}'::int[],
  'Option A (Continuous model monitoring for drift and performance degradation) is correct because models can degrade over time due to changes in data distribution (data drift) or concept drift, requiring ongoing observation. Option B (Regular retraining of the model with new data) is also correct, as models need to be updated periodically to adapt to evolving patterns and maintain accuracy. Option C (Skipping data preprocessing for new data streams) is incorrect; data preprocessing is crucial for all data, including new streams, to maintain data quality. Option D (Ceasing all model development once deployed) is incorrect, as ML development is an iterative process that continues post-deployment. Option E (Manually adjusting model predictions in real-time) is generally not scalable or efficient for production systems and defeats the purpose of automation.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  40,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_73',
  'A company is preparing a large, diverse dataset for training a new machine learning model. Which of the following data preparation steps are crucial for ensuring high model quality and performance? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Handling missing values and outliers.","Performing feature scaling or normalization.","Deploying the model to a production endpoint.","Skipping exploratory data analysis.","Optimizing hyperparameter tuning before data cleaning."]'::json,
  '{0,1}'::int[],
  'Option A (Handling missing values and outliers) is correct because missing data and extreme outliers can significantly distort model training and lead to poor performance. Option B (Performing feature scaling or normalization) is also correct, as it ensures that all features contribute equally to the model and can prevent issues with certain algorithms (e.g., gradient descent-based models). Option C (Deploying the model to a production endpoint) is a post-training step, not a data preparation step. Option D (Skipping exploratory data analysis) is incorrect, as EDA is essential to understand data characteristics and identify necessary preprocessing steps. Option E (Optimizing hyperparameter tuning before data cleaning) is incorrect; hyperparameter tuning occurs after data preparation and often after initial model training.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  41,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_74',
  'Which of the following statements accurately describe characteristics or requirements of machine learning model training and inference phases? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Training typically requires significant computational resources and large datasets.","Inference is generally less computationally intensive than training.","Training is always performed in real-time on live data streams.","Inference always requires GPUs for optimal performance.","Training models is typically a one-time activity."]'::json,
  '{0,1}'::int[],
  'Option A (Training typically requires significant computational resources and large datasets) is correct, as models learn complex patterns from vast amounts of data, often leveraging GPUs or specialized hardware. Option B (Inference is generally less computationally intensive than training) is also correct, as it involves applying a pre-trained model to new data, which usually requires fewer resources than the initial training process. Option C (Training is always performed in real-time on live data streams) is incorrect; training is often an offline, batch process. Real-time training is possible but not universal. Option D (Inference always requires GPUs for optimal performance) is incorrect; while GPUs can accelerate inference, many inference tasks can be performed efficiently on CPUs, especially for smaller models or lower latency requirements. Option E (Training models is typically a one-time activity) is incorrect; ML model development is iterative, and models often need to be retrained periodically with new data to maintain performance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  42,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_75',
  'Which of the following are key activities typically performed during the data preprocessing stage of the ML development lifecycle? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Data collection from various sources","Feature engineering to transform raw data","Model training on prepared datasets","Data cleaning to handle missing values and outliers","Model deployment for inference"]'::json,
  '{1,3}'::int[],
  'Option B (Feature engineering) involves transforming raw data into features suitable for machine learning models. Option D (Data cleaning) addresses issues like missing values, inconsistencies, and outliers, which are critical steps in preparing data. Option A (Data collection) precedes preprocessing. Option C (Model training) and Option E (Model deployment) occur after data preprocessing.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  43,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_76',
  'A machine learning practitioner is evaluating a classification model. Which of these are common metrics used to assess the model''s performance? (Select THREE.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)","Accuracy","F1 Score","Area Under the Receiver Operating Characteristic Curve (AUC-ROC)","Mean Absolute Error (MAE)"]'::json,
  '{1,2,3}'::int[],
  'Option B (Accuracy), Option C (F1 Score), and Option D (AUC-ROC) are standard evaluation metrics specifically for classification models. Accuracy measures the proportion of correctly classified instances. F1 Score is the harmonic mean of precision and recall, useful for imbalanced datasets. AUC-ROC evaluates the model''s ability to distinguish between classes across various threshold settings. Option A (RMSE) and Option E (MAE) are typically used for regression models to measure prediction error.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  44,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_77',
  'Which of the following are essential stages in the machine learning development lifecycle? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Data Collection","Software Deployment","Model Training","Database Administration","Network Configuration"]'::json,
  '{0,2}'::int[],
  'Option A (Data Collection) and Option C (Model Training) are fundamental and essential stages in the machine learning development lifecycle. Data collection involves gathering relevant data, and model training is where the algorithm learns patterns from this data. Option B (Software Deployment) is a broader IT concept, not specific to the ML lifecycle stages. Option D (Database Administration) and Option E (Network Configuration) are IT infrastructure tasks that support ML but are not core ML lifecycle stages themselves.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  45,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_78',
  'A data scientist is evaluating a classification model for predicting customer churn. Which of the following metrics are commonly used to assess the performance of such a model, especially when dealing with imbalanced datasets? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Accuracy","Precision","Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)","F1 Score","Mean Absolute Error (MAE)"]'::json,
  '{1,3}'::int[],
  'Option B (Precision) and Option D (F1 Score) are commonly used metrics for evaluating classification models, particularly when dealing with imbalanced datasets, as they provide a more nuanced view of performance than accuracy alone. Precision measures the proportion of true positive predictions among all positive predictions. The F1 Score is the harmonic mean of precision and recall, offering a balance between the two. Option A (Accuracy) can be misleading with imbalanced datasets (anti-pattern: ap-1.3-001). Option C (Root Mean Squared Error) and Option E (Mean Absolute Error) are metrics typically used for regression problems, not classification.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  46,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_79',
  'Which of these concepts are directly related to a machine learning model''s ability to generalize to new, unseen data? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Data Normalization","Underfitting","Feature Scaling","Overfitting","Hyperparameter Tuning"]'::json,
  '{1,3}'::int[],
  'Option B (Underfitting) and Option D (Overfitting) are two critical concepts directly related to a model''s generalization ability. Underfitting occurs when a model is too simple to capture the underlying patterns in the training data, leading to poor performance on both training and new data. Overfitting occurs when a model learns the training data too well, including noise, and performs poorly on new data. Option A (Data Normalization), Option C (Feature Scaling), and Option E (Hyperparameter Tuning) are techniques used to improve model performance and generalization, but they are not the concepts of generalization themselves.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  47,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_80',
  'After deploying a machine learning model into production, which of the following activities are crucial for maintaining its effectiveness over time? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Continuous Model Monitoring","Initial Data Labeling","Regular Model Retraining","One-time Model Evaluation","Algorithm Selection"]'::json,
  '{0,2}'::int[],
  'Option A (Continuous Model Monitoring) and Option C (Regular Model Retraining) are crucial post-deployment activities for maintaining a model''s effectiveness. Models can degrade over time due to data drift or concept drift, making continuous monitoring essential to detect performance issues. Regular retraining with fresh data helps the model adapt to new patterns (anti-pattern: ap-1.3-003). Option B (Initial Data Labeling), Option D (One-time Model Evaluation), and Option E (Algorithm Selection) are all part of the initial development lifecycle, not ongoing post-deployment maintenance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  48,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_5_m_5_3_81',
  'A company is preparing a large, raw dataset for training a new machine learning model. Which of the following steps are fundamental to ensuring the data is suitable for model consumption and can significantly impact model performance? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Model Deployment","Data Preprocessing","Feature Engineering","Hyperparameter Optimization","Inference Endpoint Creation"]'::json,
  '{1,2}'::int[],
  'Option B (Data Preprocessing) and Option C (Feature Engineering) are fundamental steps in preparing raw data for machine learning and are crucial for model performance (anti-pattern: ap-1.3-002). Data preprocessing involves cleaning, transforming, and organizing raw data. Feature engineering involves creating new features or transforming existing ones to improve model accuracy. Option A (Model Deployment) and Option E (Inference Endpoint Creation) occur after a model is trained. Option D (Hyperparameter Optimization) is part of the model training and evaluation phase, not data preparation.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain5_1',
  NOW(),
  49,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_5_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

