  '["Algorithmic bias","Network latency","Human bias","Compute resource limits","Storage capacity"]'::json,
  '{0,2}'::int[],
  'Option A (Algorithmic bias) and Option C (Human bias) are recognized sources of bias in AI systems, along with data bias. Algorithmic bias can arise from the model''s design or training process, while human bias can be introduced through data labeling or problem formulation. Option B (Network latency), Option D (Compute resource limits), and Option E (Storage capacity) are infrastructure or performance concerns, not direct sources of bias in the AI model itself.',
