  'Option B (Financial industry regulations for credit scoring models) often require transparency and explainability to ensure fair and non-discriminatory lending practices. Option D (GDPR''s right to explanation) grants individuals the right to receive meaningful information about the logic involved in automated decision-making. Option A (AWS Well-Architected Framework principles) provides best practices for cloud architecture but is not a regulatory requirement. Option C (HIPAA) focuses on healthcare data privacy and security, not specifically AI explainability. Option E (PCI DSS) is for payment card data security, not AI explainability.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain8_1',
  NOW(),
  49,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_8_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_8_m_8_2_100',
  'When developing AI systems, especially those interacting with users or making critical decisions, it''s often necessary to balance the model''s safety and performance with its transparency and explainability. Which two considerations are crucial when striking this balance? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Prioritizing model performance exclusively over interpretability","Using model cards to document safety and transparency aspects","Avoiding any form of human oversight to streamline operations","Measuring interpretability alongside predictive performance","Deploying models without any safety testing to accelerate time-to-market"]'::json,
  '{1,3}'::int[],
  'Option B (Using model cards to document safety and transparency aspects) provides a structured way to communicate the model''s characteristics, including its safety features and explainability methods, aiding in transparency. Option D (Measuring interpretability alongside predictive performance) ensures that both the effectiveness and the understandability of the model are evaluated, allowing for informed trade-offs. Option A (Prioritizing performance exclusively) neglects the balance with interpretability. Option C (Avoiding human oversight) is an anti-pattern (ap-4.1-002) that compromises safety. Option E (Deploying without safety testing) is an irresponsible practice that risks harm.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain8_1',
  NOW(),
  50,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_8_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_8_m_8_2_101',
  'To build trust and ensure effective adoption of AI systems, especially those with complex underlying models, human-centered design principles are vital for creating explainable AI. Which two aspects are central to a human-centered approach for explainable AI? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Focusing solely on technical metrics of explainability for data scientists","Incorporating user feedback into the development of explainability features","Minimizing user interaction with AI explanations to prevent confusion","Designing explanations that are understandable and actionable for end-users","Automating the generation of explanations without user input"]'::json,
  '{1,3}'::int[],
  'Option B (Incorporating user feedback into the development of explainability features) ensures that the explanations are relevant and useful from the perspective of the people who will use or be affected by the AI. Option D (Designing explanations that are understandable and actionable for end-users) emphasizes making explanations accessible and practical, rather than just technically accurate, so users can make informed decisions. Option A (Focusing solely on technical metrics) neglects the user''s perspective. Option C (Minimizing user interaction) and Option E (Automating without user input) contradict the principles of human-centered design, which prioritizes user needs and involvement.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain8_1',
  NOW(),
  51,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_8_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_8_m_8_2_102',
  'Maintaining transparency in AI model development includes providing clear information about the data used for training. Which two types of information are crucial for ensuring data provenance and transparency? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Model inference latency","Licensing and usage rights of the dataset","Hyperparameter tuning results","Data source and collection methodology","GPU utilization during training"]'::json,
  '{1,3}'::int[],
  'Option B (Licensing and usage rights of the dataset) is crucial for understanding the legal and ethical boundaries of how the data can be used, ensuring compliance and transparency. Option D (Data source and collection methodology) provides critical context about where the data came from and how it was gathered, which is essential for assessing potential biases or limitations. Option A (Model inference latency), Option C (Hyperparameter tuning results), and Option E (GPU utilization during training) are related to model performance or training efficiency, not data provenance or the transparency of the dataset itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain8_1',
  NOW(),
  52,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_8_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

