  'Chain-of-Thought prompting begins by Option A (Present the problem statement to be solved). Then, Option C (Provide examples of intermediate reasoning steps) demonstrates how to break down the problem. Following the examples, Option B (Request the model to explain its reasoning steps) explicitly asks the model to show its work. Finally, Option D (Ask for the final answer after the reasoning) prompts for the conclusion.',
