  'Setting up an Amazon Bedrock Agent begins with Option A (Provide instructions for the agent''s behavior) to define its purpose and persona. Next, Option D (Associate a foundation model with the agent) connects it to the underlying LLM. Then, Option B (Define actions and action groups for the agent) specifies the tools and APIs it can use. Finally, Option C (Test the agent''s ability to perform tasks) verifies its functionality.',
