  'Choosing a vector store starts with Option D (Identify the type of data to be stored and queried) to understand the data characteristics. Then, Option B (Determine the required scale and performance for vector search) defines the technical requirements. Option C (Assess the cost implications of different vector store options) is a crucial business consideration. Lastly, Option A (Evaluate integration complexity with existing systems) ensures compatibility with the broader architecture.',
