INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_8_m_8_2_121',
  'A financial institution uses a black-box deep learning model for loan approvals. Due to regulations like GDPR, they must provide explanations for automated decisions. The data science team needs to implement post-hoc explainability using Amazon SageMaker Clarify to meet these requirements. Order the following steps to achieve this.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure SageMaker Clarify to generate SHAP values or feature importance scores.","Deploy the explainability endpoint or process the explanations.","Prepare the input data for explanation, including features and baseline values.","Identify the specific model and prediction endpoint to be explained."]'::json,
  '{3,2,0,1}'::int[],
  'To implement post-hoc explainability using Amazon SageMaker Clarify for a black-box model, a clear sequence is required. Option D (Identify the specific model and prediction endpoint to be explained) is the initial step to target the correct model. Option C (Prepare the input data for explanation, including features and baseline values) provides the necessary context for Clarify''s analysis. Option A (Configure SageMaker Clarify to generate SHAP values or feature importance scores) specifies the explainability technique. Finally, Option B (Deploy the explainability endpoint or process the explanations) makes the explanations accessible for regulatory reporting or user understanding, addressing the anti-pattern of choosing black-box models without explainability planning.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain8_1',
  NOW(),
  43,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_8_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_8_m_8_2_122',
  'A pharmaceutical company is developing an AI model to predict drug efficacy. To build trust with regulators and medical professionals, they need to create Amazon SageMaker Model Cards to document the model''s purpose, performance, and ethical considerations. Order the following key sections as they typically appear in a SageMaker Model Card.',
  'ordering',
  '["Model Details (e.g., purpose, version, training data sources).","Evaluation Results (e.g., performance metrics, fairness metrics).","Intended Uses and Ethical Considerations (e.g., limitations, risks).","Training Details (e.g., algorithms, hyperparameters, training environment)."]'::json,
  '{0,3,1,2}'::int[],
  'Amazon SageMaker Model Cards are structured to provide comprehensive documentation. Option A (Model Details) typically comes first, introducing the model''s basic information. Option D (Training Details) follows, describing how the model was built. Option B (Evaluation Results) then presents the model''s performance and fairness. Finally, Option C (Intended Uses and Ethical Considerations) outlines the model''s appropriate applications, limitations, and potential risks, ensuring transparency and responsible deployment.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain8_1',
  NOW(),
  44,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_8_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_8_m_8_2_123',
  'A data science team is tasked with explaining the predictions of a complex deep learning model. They decide to use post-hoc explainability techniques like SHAP values to understand feature contributions. Order the general steps involved in applying such a technique to a trained model.',
  'ordering',
  '["Interpret the generated explanations to understand feature importance and impact.","Select a suitable post-hoc explainability algorithm (e.g., SHAP, LIME).","Define the scope of explanation (e.g., global feature importance or local prediction explanation).","Apply the algorithm to the model and input data to generate explanations."]'::json,
  '{2,1,3,0}'::int[],
  'Applying post-hoc explainability techniques to a trained model follows a logical progression. Option C (Define the scope of explanation) is the initial step, determining whether to explain overall model behavior or specific predictions. Option B (Select a suitable post-hoc explainability algorithm) involves choosing the appropriate method. Option D (Apply the algorithm to the model and input data to generate explanations) executes the explanation process. Finally, Option A (Interpret the generated explanations to understand feature importance and impact) involves analyzing the output to gain insights into the model''s decision-making.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain8_1',
  NOW(),
  45,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_8_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_8_m_8_2_124',
  'A company is evaluating different types of machine learning models for a sensitive application. They need to understand the inherent transparency of various model architectures to comply with future explainability requirements. Order the following model types from MOST inherently transparent to LEAST inherently transparent.',
  'ordering',
  '["Deep Neural Networks (DNNs)","Linear Regression","Decision Trees","Gradient Boosting Machines (GBMs)"]'::json,
  '{1,2,3,0}'::int[],
  'Understanding the inherent transparency of model architectures is crucial for explainability. Option B (Linear Regression) is generally considered the most transparent, as feature coefficients directly indicate impact. Option C (Decision Trees) are also highly transparent, as their rules can be visualized and followed. Option D (Gradient Boosting Machines (GBMs)) are less transparent than single decision trees due to their ensemble nature, but still more interpretable than deep learning. Option A (Deep Neural Networks (DNNs)) are typically considered black-box models due to their complex, non-linear structures, making them the least inherently transparent.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain8_1',
  NOW(),
  46,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_8_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_8_m_8_2_125',
  'A healthcare startup is developing an AI system to assist clinicians with early disease detection. To foster trust and adoption, the system must be explainable to medical professionals. Order the following steps to apply human-centered design principles to create an explainable AI system that users trust.',
  'ordering',
  '["Involve clinicians in the design and evaluation of explanation interfaces.","Identify the specific information clinicians need to trust and act on AI recommendations.","Iteratively refine explanation methods based on user feedback and usability testing.","Develop explanation interfaces that present model reasoning in an understandable format."]'::json,
  '{1,0,3,2}'::int[],
  'Creating an explainable AI system that users trust through human-centered design involves a specific sequence. Option B (Identify the specific information clinicians need to trust and act on AI recommendations) is the foundational step, understanding user requirements. Option A (Involve clinicians in the design and evaluation of explanation interfaces) ensures user input from the start. Option D (Develop explanation interfaces that present model reasoning in an understandable format) translates the technical explanations into a user-friendly format. Finally, Option C (Iteratively refine explanation methods based on user feedback and usability testing) ensures continuous improvement and alignment with user needs.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain8_1',
  NOW(),
  47,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_8_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_8_m_8_2_126',
  'A data science team is evaluating a new deep learning model for a critical application. They need to balance the model''s performance and safety with the requirement for transparency and explainability. Order the following steps to effectively achieve this balance.',
  'ordering',
  '["Prioritize model safety and performance metrics.","Implement explainability techniques (e.g., SHAP, feature importance) to understand model behavior.","Analyze trade-offs between model complexity, performance, and interpretability.","Communicate model limitations and explainability insights to stakeholders."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}'::int[],
  'Balancing model safety, performance, and transparency requires a thoughtful approach. Option A (Prioritize model safety and performance metrics) establishes the primary goals. Option B (Implement explainability techniques (e.g., SHAP, feature importance) to understand model behavior) provides insights into the model''s decision-making. Option C (Analyze trade-offs between model complexity, performance, and interpretability) involves making informed decisions about model choice. Finally, Option D (Communicate model limitations and explainability insights to stakeholders) ensures transparency and manages expectations, fostering trust.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain8_1',
  NOW(),
  48,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_8_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_8_m_8_2_127',
  'A company is building a machine learning model for a regulated industry and needs to ensure that the data used for training and inference has clear provenance. This is crucial for auditing and explainability. Order the following steps to establish and maintain data provenance for an ML model.',
  'ordering',
  '["Document all data transformations and preprocessing steps.","Implement version control for datasets used in training.","Record the origin and source of all raw data.","Store metadata about data collection and licensing."]'::json,
  '{2,3,1,0}'::int[],
  'Establishing and maintaining data provenance for an ML model is essential for transparency and auditability. Option C (Record the origin and source of all raw data) is the foundational step, identifying where the data came from. Option D (Store metadata about data collection and licensing) provides crucial context and legal information. Option B (Implement version control for datasets used in training) ensures that specific data versions can be tracked. Finally, Option A (Document all data transformations and preprocessing steps) provides a clear history of how the data was prepared for the model, completing the provenance trail.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain8_1',
  NOW(),
  49,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_8_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_8_m_8_2_128',
  'A data science team has deployed an ML model into production and wants to continuously monitor its explainability to detect any shifts in feature importance or model behavior over time. Order the following steps to implement post-deployment explainability monitoring using Amazon SageMaker Clarify.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure SageMaker Clarify to generate explainability baselines from the trained model.","Set up a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule to continuously analyze explainability metrics.","Define the features and target for explainability monitoring.","Analyze monitoring reports for deviations in feature importance or model drift."]'::json,
  '{2,0,1,3}'::int[],
  'Implementing post-deployment explainability monitoring with Amazon SageMaker Clarify requires a specific sequence. Option C (Define the features and target for explainability monitoring) is the initial setup to specify what aspects of the model''s explanations need to be tracked. Option A (Configure SageMaker Clarify to generate explainability baselines from the trained model) establishes a reference point for normal model behavior. Option B (Set up a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule to continuously analyze explainability metrics) automates the ongoing evaluation. Finally, Option D (Analyze monitoring reports for deviations in feature importance or model drift) involves reviewing the output to identify any concerning changes in model interpretability.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain8_1',
  NOW(),
  50,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_8_2',
