  'Classification (left: 0) is an ML task where the goal is to predict a discrete, categorical output (e.g., spam or not spam). Regression (left: 1) aims to predict a continuous numerical value (e.g., house prices). Clustering (left: 2) is an unsupervised learning technique used to group data points that are similar to each other, without prior knowledge of the groups.',
