  'Hallucinations refer to instances where an LLM generates plausible-sounding but factually incorrect or nonsensical information. Knowledge Cutoff describes the point in time beyond which an LLM''s training data does not extend, meaning it lacks information about more recent events. Context Limits define the maximum amount of text (in tokens) that an LLM can process or generate in a single interaction.',
