  'Hallucinations (left: 0) refer to LLMs generating plausible but incorrect or fabricated information. Knowledge cutoff (left: 1) means that base models are limited by the date of their training data and cannot access information beyond that point. Context limits (left: 2) define the finite amount of input and output tokens an LLM can process in a single interaction.',
