  NOW(),
  27,
  '{"left":["Knowledge Bases","Model Evaluation","Agents"],"right":["Automates multi-step tasks with FMs.","Manages data for RAG applications.","Assesses FM performance with metrics."]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_7_1',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_7_m_7_1_94',
  'Match each foundation model selection criterion to its definition.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Latency","B":"Context window","C":"Modality"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Latency (left item 0) refers to the time it takes for a foundation model to process an input and generate a response, which is critical for real-time applications. The context window (left item 1) defines the maximum number of tokens (words or subwords) that a model can process in a single input, impacting its ability to handle long documents or conversations. Modality (left item 2) describes the type of data a model is designed to handle, such as text, images, audio, or a combination (multi-modal).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain7_1',
  NOW(),
  28,
  '{"left":["Latency","Context window","Modality"],"right":["Time for response generation","Maximum input token length","Type of data processed (text, image)"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_7_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_7_m_7_1_95',
  'Match each foundation model customization approach to its primary characteristic.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Prompt engineering","B":"Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)","C":"Fine-tuning"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Prompt engineering (left item 0) involves crafting effective prompts to guide a pre-trained model without modifying its underlying weights, relying on in-context learning. Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) (left item 1) enhances a model''s responses by retrieving relevant information from an external knowledge base before generating an answer. Fine-tuning (left item 2) involves updating a pre-trained model''s weights using a specific dataset to adapt it to a particular task or domain.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain7_1',
  NOW(),
  29,
  '{"left":["Prompt engineering","Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)","Fine-tuning"],"right":["No model changes, in-context learning","External knowledge retrieval","Model weights updated with new data"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_7_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_7_m_7_1_96',
  'Match the vector store service to its underlying database technology.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Amazon OpenSearch Service","B":"Amazon Aurora","C":"Amazon Neptune"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Amazon OpenSearch Service (left item 0) is a managed service that makes it easy to deploy, operate, and scale search and analytics workloads, including vector search capabilities. Amazon Aurora (left item 1) is a MySQL and PostgreSQL-compatible relational database built for the cloud, which can support vector embeddings through extensions like pgvector. Amazon Neptune (left item 2) is a fast, reliable, fully managed graph database service, which can also be used to store and query vector embeddings in a graph context.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain7_1',
  NOW(),
  30,
  '{"left":["Amazon OpenSearch Service","Amazon Aurora","Amazon Neptune"],"right":["Managed search and analytics","Managed relational database","Managed graph database"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_7_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_7_m_7_1_97',
  'Match the foundation model inference parameter to its effect on generated output.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Temperature","B":"Max tokens","C":"Top P"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Temperature (left item 0) is an inference parameter that controls the randomness or creativity of the model''s output; a higher temperature leads to more diverse and creative responses, while a lower temperature makes responses more deterministic. Max tokens (left item 1) sets the maximum number of tokens the model will generate in its response, effectively limiting the output length. Top P (left item 2), also known as nucleus sampling, filters out less probable tokens, considering only the smallest set of tokens whose cumulative probability exceeds the ''P'' threshold.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain7_1',
  NOW(),
  31,
  '{"left":["Temperature","Max tokens","Top P"],"right":["Controls randomness/creativity","Limits output length","Filters less probable tokens"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_7_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_7_m_7_1_98',
  'A company is selecting foundation models for different tasks. Match the task requirement to the most appropriate model size or type, considering cost and latency tradeoffs.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Simple text classification","B":"Creative content generation","C":"Summarizing long legal documents"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'For simple text classification (left item 0), a smaller, faster model is generally more cost-effective and provides lower latency, as the task does not require extensive generative capabilities (ap-3.1-001). Creative content generation (left item 1) often benefits from a larger, more powerful model due to its broader knowledge and ability to generate more nuanced and imaginative outputs. Summarizing long legal documents (left item 2) requires a model with a large context window to process the entire document effectively and maintain coherence.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain7_1',
  NOW(),
  32,
  '{"left":["Simple text classification","Creative content generation","Summarizing long legal documents"],"right":["Smaller, faster model","Larger, more powerful model","Model with large context window"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_7_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_7_m_7_1_99',
  'Match the Amazon Bedrock feature to its primary purpose in building foundation model applications.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases","B":"Amazon Bedrock Agents","C":"Amazon Bedrock Model Evaluation"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases (left item 0) are used to ground foundation models with proprietary data, enabling them to generate more accurate and relevant responses by retrieving information from specified data sources. Amazon Bedrock Agents (left item 1) are designed to automate multi-step tasks by orchestrating foundation models, tools, and data sources. Amazon Bedrock Model Evaluation (left item 2) provides tools and features for assessing the performance of foundation models against various metrics and business objectives.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain7_1',
  NOW(),
  33,
  '{"left":["Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases","Amazon Bedrock Agents","Amazon Bedrock Model Evaluation"],"right":["Grounding models with proprietary data","Automating multi-step tasks","Assessing model performance"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_7_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_7_m_7_1_100',
  'Match the foundation model customization approach to its typical cost and effort level.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Prompt engineering","B":"In-context learning (few-shot)","C":"Fine-tuning"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Prompt engineering (left item 0) typically incurs the lowest cost and minimal effort as it only involves crafting the input prompt without modifying the model itself. In-context learning, such as few-shot prompting (left item 1), has moderate cost and requires some data preparation for the examples, but still avoids model retraining. Fine-tuning (left item 2) generally involves the highest cost and significant effort due to the need for substantial high-quality training data and compute resources to update model weights.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain7_1',
  NOW(),
  34,
  '{"left":["Prompt engineering","In-context learning (few-shot)","Fine-tuning"],"right":["Lowest cost, minimal effort","Moderate cost, some data preparation","Highest cost, significant data and compute"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_7_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

