  '{"A":"Encryption at Rest","B":"Private Endpoints","C":"Access Control"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Encryption at Rest (left item 0) is a method of securing stored data (right item 0), such as training datasets and model artifacts, by encrypting it when it is not actively being used. Private Endpoints (left item 1), often implemented with Amazon VPC, are used for restricting network exposure (right item 1) of AI inference services to the public internet. Access Control (left item 2), managed by services like AWS IAM, focuses on limiting resource usage (right item 2) to authorized users and roles.',
