  NULL,
  'Amazon SageMaker Role Manager (left item 0) simplifies the management of IAM roles and permissions for SageMaker users and projects, offering a more streamlined approach than manual IAM configuration. AWS IAM Roles (left item 1) are identities that you can create in your account that have specific permissions and are designed to be assumed by trusted entities, such as users or services, to grant temporary access. AWS IAM Policies (left item 2) are JSON documents that define permissions for an IAM identity or resource, specifying what actions are allowed or denied on which resources.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain9_1',
  NOW(),
  25,
  '{"left":["Amazon SageMaker Role Manager","AWS IAM Roles","AWS IAM Policies"],"right":["Simplified SageMaker access management","Assumable identities with permissions","JSON documents defining permissions"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
