VALUES (
  'q_9_m_9_2_144',
  'A financial services firm is deploying an AI system to automate investment advice. This system must adhere to strict financial regulations (e.g., GDPR, CCPA, PCI DSS, specific financial industry acts) regarding data privacy, security, and algorithmic transparency. Match the regulatory framework to its primary focus.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"GDPR","B":"HIPAA","C":"EU AI Act"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'GDPR (General Data Protection Regulation) (left item 0) is a comprehensive data privacy and protection law in the European Union and European Economic Area, focusing on how personal data is collected, processed, and stored. HIPAA (Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act) (left item 1) is a US law that sets standards for the security, privacy, and transmission of electronic protected health information. The EU AI Act (left item 2) is a proposed regulation by the European Union that aims to establish a legal framework for AI, categorizing AI systems by risk level and imposing obligations on providers and users.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain9_1',
  NOW(),
  44,
  '{"left":["GDPR","HIPAA","EU AI Act"],"right":["Data privacy and protection","Healthcare data security","Comprehensive AI regulation"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_9_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_9_m_9_2_145',
  'A data analytics company uses various datasets to train its AI models. To ensure data quality, trustworthiness, and compliance, they need to track the origin, transformations, and usage history of all data assets feeding into their AI systems. Match the data governance concept to its definition.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Data Lineage","B":"Consent Management","C":"Data Minimization"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Data Lineage (left item 0) is the process of tracking the entire lifecycle of data, including its origin, where it moves over time, and what transformations it undergoes. Consent Management (left item 1) involves obtaining, recording, and managing individuals'' permissions for the collection, processing, and sharing of their personal data. Data Minimization (left item 2) is a principle that states organizations should only collect, process, and store the minimum amount of personal data necessary to achieve a specific purpose, reducing privacy risks.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain9_1',
  NOW(),
  45,
  '{"left":["Data Lineage","Consent Management","Data Minimization"],"right":["Tracking data origin and transformations","Managing data usage permissions","Limiting data collection to necessity"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_9_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_9_m_9_2_146',
  'An insurance company is using an AI model for claims processing. The risk management department requires thorough documentation of the model''s development, testing, and deployment to assess potential risks, ensure fairness, and justify decisions to regulators. Match the model risk management component to its objective.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Model Documentation","B":"Risk Assessment","C":"Performance Monitoring"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Model Documentation (left item 0) involves creating and maintaining detailed records of an AI model''s design, development, training data, evaluation, and deployment, which is crucial for transparency, auditability, and regulatory compliance. Risk Assessment (left item 1) is the process of identifying, analyzing, and evaluating potential risks associated with an AI model, such as bias, fairness, security vulnerabilities, or unintended consequences. Performance Monitoring (left item 2) involves continuously tracking an AI model''s output, accuracy, and other key metrics in production to detect drift, degradation, or anomalous behavior.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain9_1',
  NOW(),
  46,
  '{"left":["Model Documentation","Risk Assessment","Performance Monitoring"],"right":["Comprehensive record of model lifecycle","Identify and evaluate model risks","Continuous evaluation of model behavior"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_9_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_9_m_9_2_147',
  'A large tech company develops an internal AI tool to optimize employee task assignments. The development team argues that since it''s an internal tool, extensive governance frameworks like model cards or audit logs are unnecessary, prioritizing rapid deployment. The governance team disagrees. Match the governance concept to its relevance for internal AI tools.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Internal AI Governance","B":"Audit Trails","C":"Bias Detection"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Internal AI Governance (left item 0) is essential for all AI tools, even internal ones, because they can still impact employees through biased recommendations or performance evaluations, making governance a best practice regardless of customer-facing status. Audit Trails (left item 1) are critical for internal AI tools to record system actions, providing transparency, accountability, and a means to investigate issues or demonstrate compliance. Bias Detection (left item 2) is important for internal AI tools to identify and mitigate unfair outcomes that could affect employees, ensuring equitable treatment.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain9_1',
  NOW(),
  47,
  '{"left":["Internal AI Governance","Audit Trails","Bias Detection"],"right":["Essential for all AI tools","Record of system actions","Identify unfair outcomes"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_9_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_9_m_9_2_148',
  'A multinational corporation needs to continuously monitor its AI systems for compliance with various industry standards and internal policies. They require an automated service to collect evidence and generate audit reports for regulatory bodies, ensuring that all AI-related configurations and operations meet the necessary requirements. Match the AWS service to its primary compliance and audit function.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"AWS Audit Manager","B":"AWS Config","C":"AWS CloudTrail"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'AWS Audit Manager (left item 0) helps you continuously audit your AWS usage to simplify how you assess risk and compliance with regulations and industry standards. It automates evidence collection, making it easier to generate audit reports. AWS Config (left item 1) continuously monitors and records your AWS resource configurations and allows you to automate the evaluation of recorded configurations against desired configurations, providing a history of changes. AWS CloudTrail (left item 2) provides a record of actions taken by a user, role, or an AWS service, logging API calls and related events, which is crucial for security analysis and operational troubleshooting.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain9_1',
  NOW(),
  48,
  '{"left":["AWS Audit Manager","AWS Config","AWS CloudTrail"],"right":["Automated compliance evidence collection","Resource configuration change tracking","API activity and event logging"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_9_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_9_m_9_2_149',
  'A research institution is collecting and processing large volumes of data for AI model training. Due to data privacy regulations (e.g., GDPR) and storage cost considerations, they need to define and enforce specific retention periods for different categories of data used by their AI systems. Match the data governance principle to its definition.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Data Retention Policy","B":"Data Minimization","C":"Data Anonymization"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'A Data Retention Policy (left item 0) defines how long specific types of data should be stored, based on legal, regulatory, and business requirements, and ensures data is securely disposed of after its retention period. Data Minimization (left item 1) is a principle that advocates for collecting and processing only the personal data that is strictly necessary for a specific purpose, reducing the scope of potential data breaches. Data Anonymization (left item 2) is the process of removing or modifying personally identifiable information from data so that the data subject cannot be identified, helping to protect privacy while allowing data use.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain9_1',
  NOW(),
  49,
  '{"left":["Data Retention Policy","Data Minimization","Data Anonymization"],"right":["Rules for data storage duration","Limit data collection to necessity","Remove identifiable information from data"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_9_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_9_m_9_2_150',
  'A media company is integrating a generative AI model from Amazon Bedrock into its content creation workflow. To ensure brand safety and prevent the generation of harmful, off-topic, or inappropriate content, they need to implement strong content moderation and safety controls. Match the generative AI concept or service to its primary function.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Amazon Bedrock Guardrails","B":"Prompt Engineering","C":"Content Filtering"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Amazon Bedrock Guardrails (left item 0) allow you to implement safety policies for your generative AI applications, defining custom denied topics and content filters to ensure outputs align with brand guidelines and safety standards. Prompt Engineering (left item 1) is the art and science of designing effective inputs (prompts) for generative AI models to elicit desired responses and guide their behavior. Content Filtering (left item 2) is a general mechanism used to block or flag undesirable content, which can be implemented as part of a guardrail or a separate post-processing step to ensure outputs meet safety and quality criteria.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain9_1',
  NOW(),
  50,
  '{"left":["Amazon Bedrock Guardrails","Prompt Engineering","Content Filtering"],"right":["Implement safety policies for generative AI","Designing effective model inputs","Blocking undesirable output"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_9_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_9_m_9_2_151',
  'An e-commerce platform uses an AI system to dynamically adjust product pricing. To ensure fairness, detect potential manipulation, and comply with regulatory scrutiny, all decisions made by the AI system, along with associated inputs and outputs, must be meticulously recorded and easily retrievable for review. Match the governance mechanism to its role in this scenario.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Audit Logs","B":"Model Monitoring","C":"Data Governance"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Audit Logs (left item 0) are crucial for recording all actions, inputs, and outputs of the AI system, providing an immutable record for accountability, debugging, and demonstrating compliance to regulators. Model Monitoring (left item 1) involves continuously tracking the AI model''s performance, drift, and fairness metrics in production to ensure it operates as expected and to detect any anomalous behavior or biases. Data Governance (left item 2) encompasses the overall management of data availability, usability, integrity, and security, including defining policies for data lineage, quality, and retention, which are foundational for trustworthy AI systems.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain9_1',
  NOW(),
  51,
  '{"left":["Audit Logs","Model Monitoring","Data Governance"],"right":["Record AI system actions and events","Track model performance and behavior","Manage data lifecycle and quality"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_9_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

